{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1472248-kindred-of-the-east-record-of-the-hungry-dead-a-rebuild-of-kote","id":1472248,"title":"[Kindred of the East] Record of the Hungry Dead: A Rebuild of KotE","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-11T11:38:16-08:00","id":1472248,"title":"[Kindred of the East] Record of the Hungry Dead: A Rebuild of KotE","content":"Fans of the erstwhile Ten Thousand Demons, gather round: I've written a systems reboot for Kindred of the East on the ST Vault.<br /> <br /> <i>Record of the Hungry Dead </i>is built around the V20 rules, and it keeps the original concept-- the dead demon immortals, escapees of hell who are repaying their karmic debts. But it streamlines systems significantly, making the game a lot easier to explain and play:<ul><li>New and redesigned Arts (Disciplines)</li> <li>A brand-new system for Virtues, Chi, and Soul Imbalance that draws on baseline V20 rules</li> <li>New innate abilities and Backgrounds</li> <li>NPCs from across the modern history of East Asia</li> </ul>It's all here, and it's Pay What You Want (meaning free unless you feel like giving me a tip). I'm proud of it and I think it can lead to some good KotE gaming for people in the future, so I appreciate any attention you can throw my way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/383100/Record-of-the-Hungry-Dead-A-Rebuild-of-Kindred-of-the-East\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/383100.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/383100/Record-of-the-Hungry-Dead-A-Rebuild-of-Kindred-of-the-East\" target=\"_blank\"> Record of the Hungry Dead: A Rebuild of Kindred of the East - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/383100/Record-of-the-Hungry-Dead-A-Rebuild-of-Kindred-of-the-East\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/383100/Record-of-the-Hungry-Dead-A-Rebuild-of-Kindred-of-the-East </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Record of the Hungry Dead: A Rebuild of Kindred of the East - Note: This book is part of the earlier \"first edition\" cycle of&nbsp;Kindred of the East: The Relentless Age, covering syst </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If you're interested, the book is intended to synergize with a setting reboot I wrote last year called <i>Analects of the Damned</i>-- which is also Pay What You Want:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/341889/Analects-of-the-Damned\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/341889.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/341889/Analects-of-the-Damned\" target=\"_blank\"> Analects of the Damned - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/341889/Analects-of-the-Damned\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/341889/Analects-of-the-Damned </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Analects of the Damned - Revisit the Game of Blood and Enlightenment In 1998, White Wolf Games released Kindred of the East, the flagship supplem </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T12:40:47-08:00","id":1472254,"title":"","content":"Does it address the setting issues with Wan Kuei that makes it such a contested piece of the world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T13:17:50-08:00","id":1472260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1472248-kindred-of-the-east-record-of-the-hungry-dead-a-rebuild-of-kote?p=1472254#post1472254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does it address the setting issues with Wan Kuei that makes it such a contested piece of the world?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Analects of the Damned</i> does.<br /> <br /> In short, Cainites and Hungry Dead technically exist everywhere, but Hungry Dead<i> society</i> is dominant in Asia due to having the time and resources to establish itself there-- the main resource being a relatively stable and widespread human society, which the Hungry Dead really need to thrive (even more so than Cainites), and which they were lucky to get in the form of the Chinese imperial state.<br /> <br /> In places like Japan, there's a thorny history between the Hungry Dead and the native &quot;Cainite&quot; bloodlines that is beginning to come to a head with younger generations. But there is no Great Leap Outward, and no ingrained hatred of foreigners beyond regular old prejudices-- In the modern nights, it's just two species of vampires warily circling each other and navigating each other's worlds, now that there are planes and trains for them to bump into each other much more often than before.<br /> <br /> <i>Record of the Hungry Dead</i>, though, is much more about systems, with flavor text being the extent of its setting details. Hope that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T15:28:51-08:00","id":1472271,"title":"","content":"Well done Hsienfan, excellent work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3399-hachiman","name":"hachiman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3399_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T18:25:24-08:00","id":1472286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hachiman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1472248-kindred-of-the-east-record-of-the-hungry-dead-a-rebuild-of-kote?p=1472271#post1472271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well done Hsienfan, excellent work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much! Glad you enjoyed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T10:47:46-08:00","id":1472317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hsienfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1472248-kindred-of-the-east-record-of-the-hungry-dead-a-rebuild-of-kote?p=1472260#post1472260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, Cainites and Hungry Dead technically exist everywhere...</div> </div> </div> </div>So we could play Hungry Dead from America, Canada, France, etc? Interesting. Are there rules for this in AotD?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-12T12:23:49-08:00","id":1472321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1472248-kindred-of-the-east-record-of-the-hungry-dead-a-rebuild-of-kote?p=1472317#post1472317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we could play Hungry Dead from America, Canada, France, etc? Interesting. Are there rules for this in AotD?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Analects of the Damned</i> is setting-only and is limited to Asian locales (specifically China, Japan, and Korea, with only a brief mention of India). <i>Record of the Hungry Dead</i> is where the rules are, and those also assume an Asian setting in your games.<br /> <br /> However, I'm happy to help right now. If you want to play a Hungry Dead in a setting outside of Asia and its Hungry Dead societies, use the rules in <i>Record of the Hungry Dead,</i> but keep the following in mind:<ul><li>Characters are in Cainite territory and very likely believe themselves to be Caitiff, in the absence of mentors who can sniff out their true nature. Their memories of hell, if they haven't been suppressed, are fragmented and confusing.</li> <li>Virtue abilities and soul imbalance rules are the same, but they are instinctual and will not be recognized for what they are.</li> <li>Character creation is the same, but default to Humanity 7 for a starting character who has just regained a grip on themselves. When necessary (like rolling for Humanity loss), substitute Cainite Virtues with Hungry Dead Virtues as shown by the mortal NPC in <i>Record of the Hungry Dead.</i></li> <li>It is also possible to follow a Path, which will function like Dharma for the character: Assign the Path an appropriate associated Virtue, start them at Path level 1, then follow the Dharma rules.</li> <li>Demon Arts can naturally manifest and be developed without a teacher, as those capacities come from their time in hell (though the third eye that manifests when using Tears of Hell will be... problematic).</li> <li>Characters are very unlikely to possess Godbody Arts, unless trained by someone with a background in the Dharmas.</li> <li>Characters can kludge together a de facto knowledge of some Soul Arts, if given tutelage in a close Cainite equivalent. They won't be able to learn Necromancy, for example, but training in it may open them up to Lesser Ghost Mantle. The regular Soul Art rules still apply.</li> </ul>Hope that helps for now. I can see this is an area where I could write an update, so thank you for the insight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}